WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.097 --> 00:00:15.562
Tang Monk looked at the robbers.

2
00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:17.182
He was shaking.

3
00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:20.244
s-sorry," he said.

4
00:00:20.264 --> 00:00:22.905
"But we're just monks.

5
00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:24.445
We don't have any money."

6
00:00:25.666 --> 00:00:28.327
give us whatever else you have," said one robber.

7
00:00:29.227 --> 00:00:31.424
He came closer.

8
00:00:31.484 --> 00:00:32.925
"Please, sir," said the monk.

9
00:00:32.945 --> 00:00:35.907
"We—" put up his hand.

10
00:00:36.568 --> 00:00:38.129
"I'll deal with these robbers, Master."

11
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.550
approached the men.

12
00:00:41.511 --> 00:00:44.433
They all laughed.

13
00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:47.435
"Look at the little monkey!"

14
00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:48.476
said one of them.

15
00:00:50.257 --> 00:00:51.238
laughed too.

16
00:00:51.258 --> 00:00:53.620
"Yes, I am a monkey.

17
00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.401
I am rather small, it's true."

18
00:00:57.382 --> 00:01:00.748
He removed the iron bar from his ear.

19
00:01:00.808 --> 00:01:02.569
"But you should be scared of me anyway."

20
00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:07.310
His iron bar grew, and his eyes flashed red with anger.

21
00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:11.631
"The monkey is a spirit!"

22
00:01:11.851 --> 00:01:12.672
cried one man.

23
00:01:12.692 --> 00:01:15.072
"Run!" cried another.

24
00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:19.173
The robbers tripped over one another, trying to get away.

25
00:01:19.193 --> 00:01:23.715
Wukong raised the iron bar, ready to strike.

26
00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:26.696
Wukong!" cried the Tang Monk.

27
00:01:26.716 --> 00:01:28.824
"Don't hurt them!"

28
00:01:28.944 --> 00:01:30.946
Wukong turned around as the men ran away.

29
00:01:32.307 --> 00:01:33.348
not?" he asked.

30
00:01:34.029 --> 00:01:35.129
"They were going to hurt us."

31
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.892
"A Buddhist monk never hurts people," said the monk.

32
00:01:39.873 --> 00:01:42.035
"I would rather get hurt than hurt someone else."

33
00:01:44.877 --> 00:01:47.319
laughed. "That's ridiculous.

34
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.201
We should have beaten them up!"

35
00:01:50.181 --> 00:01:51.523
Tang Monk shook his head.

36
00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:54.465
"You are cruel and violent, Wukong."

37
00:01:55.926 --> 00:01:56.506
was angry.

38
00:01:56.527 --> 00:01:58.188
"I just saved your life!"

39
00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:58.860
he cried.

40
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.321
"How dare you scold me!"

41
00:02:02.401 --> 00:02:03.041
He paused.

42
00:02:03.061 --> 00:02:06.062
"I don't have to accept this treatment.

43
00:02:06.702 --> 00:02:07.202
I'm leaving!"

44
00:02:08.603 --> 00:02:11.264
Wukong leaped into the air and was gone.

45
00:02:15.845 --> 00:02:19.486
The Tang Monk sighed and then continued his journey.

46
00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:24.527
Later that day he saw an old woman.

47
00:02:24.547 --> 00:02:27.368
"Monk," said the woman.

48
00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:28.965
"Where are you going?"

49
00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:32.887
"I'm going to the Western Paradise," said the Tang Monk.

50
00:02:34.288 --> 00:02:36.009
"Don't you have anyone with you?"

51
00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:36.970
asked the woman.

52
00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.532
"You can't go there alone."

53
00:02:39.552 --> 00:02:42.974
"I did have a companion," said the Tang Monk.

54
00:02:42.994 --> 00:02:46.096
"But he got angry when I scolded him for being violent.

55
00:02:46.676 --> 00:02:47.177
He left."

56
00:02:48.378 --> 00:02:51.420
"Your companion will come back," said the woman.

57
00:02:57.183 --> 00:03:00.437
he does, trick him into putting this on."

58
00:03:01.457 --> 00:03:04.198
She pulled a metal headband out of her bag.

59
00:03:04.218 --> 00:03:09.579
"Whenever he misbehaves, recite the Tight Headband spell."

60
00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.701
The old woman whispered a magical spell to the Tang Monk.

61
00:03:17.081 --> 00:03:18.422
you," said the Tang Monk.

62
00:03:18.442 --> 00:03:26.964
"But how did There was a flash of bright light, and the woman rose into the air.

63
00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.101
"The bodhisattva Guanyin!"

64
00:03:30.401 --> 00:03:31.402
cried the Tang Monk.

65
00:03:32.223 --> 00:03:34.405
He got down from his horse and bowed.

66
00:03:37.047 --> 00:03:41.591
Meanwhile Wukong sat in the palace of the Dragon King of the Eastern Sea.

67
00:03:42.492 --> 00:03:44.834
He and the Dragon King were drinking tea.

68
00:03:44.854 --> 00:03:49.818
"I hope you've learned from your punishment," said the Dragon King.

69
00:03:49.838 --> 00:03:53.201
"Yes, I have," said Wukong.

70
00:03:53.221 --> 00:03:56.784
"I won't cause any more trouble for the Jade Emperor."

71
00:03:57.876 --> 00:03:59.677
Dragon King sipped his tea.

72
00:03:59.697 --> 00:04:02.058
"What will you do now?"

73
00:04:02.138 --> 00:04:07.361
"I was traveling west with a monk, to get scriptures from Buddha," said Wukong.

74
00:04:07.381 --> 00:04:09.743
"I promised Guanyin I would do it."

75
00:04:10.643 --> 00:04:12.224
The Dragon King smiled.

76
00:04:12.244 --> 00:04:13.805
"That's wonderful!"

77
00:04:14.805 --> 00:04:15.786
Wukong shrugged.

78
00:04:15.806 --> 00:04:18.187
"Yes, well, I'm not doing it anymore."

79
00:04:19.408 --> 00:04:21.469
The Dragon King put down his teacup.

80
00:04:22.249 --> 00:04:22.870
"Why not?"

81
00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:26.752
"That monk had a bad attitude," said Wukong.

82
00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:29.289
yelled at me.

83
00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.211
He said I was cruel and violent."

84
00:04:37.214 --> 00:04:39.195
Dragon King coughed nervously.

85
00:04:39.215 --> 00:04:42.538
"Well, Wukong.

86
00:04:42.898 --> 00:04:44.199
The monk has a point."

87
00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:46.880
glared at the king.

88
00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.702
"What do you mean?"

89
00:04:50.083 --> 00:04:54.245
king hesitated and then said, "You violent sometimes."

90
00:04:55.326 --> 00:04:57.728
Wukong folded his arms and looked at the ground.

91
00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.182
The Dragon King continued.

92
00:05:00.202 --> 00:05:04.246
"Not only that, but you made a promise to Guanyin.

93
00:05:05.488 --> 00:05:08.972
Perhaps, Wukong, it is you who has a bad attitude?"
